# Jaguar Mark X four-door saloon, 1961-1970.
#
# The wide, low large Jaguar with independent rear suspension, four round
# headlamps in pairs and a broad grille. The 4.2-litre Mark X and the 420G are
# the same shell and are represented together.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_Mark_X
#
# Dimensions 5.13 x 1.94 x 1.38 m, wheelbase 3.05 m.
#
# Shape reference: no true level side elevation exists; the best is a 420G at
# 10-15 degrees off perpendicular. The flank is reconciled against the front
# and rear three-quarters within the published dimensions. No detail image.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK brochure was consulted. British Racing Green,
# Black, Opalescent Silver Grey and Carmen Red are period Jaguar finishes.
# Weights 3, 2, 2, 1, total 8, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 200 km/h. Comfort 85/458, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 85. Class 4.
# Dates 1961-1970 production, road tail staggered 1978-1980.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-mk10.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-mk10.dae. References: citycars/references/jaguar-mk10/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the 420G flank photograph is more oblique than the pack
# notes suggest, so the flank was reconciled against both three-quarters and the
# published dimensions rather than treated as a true side elevation. Grille,
# four-lamp and bumper detail is simplified at sprite scale.


obj=citycar
name=JaguarMk10(BritishRacingGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1961
intro_month=10
retire_year=1980
retire_month=6
speed=200
length=3
class=4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=85
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=458

